snp3.5:1.1 | S: So I have heard. | T: I have heard that
snp3.5:1.2 | S: At one time the Buddha was staying near Rājagaha, on the Vulture’s Peak Mountain. | T: on one occasion the Blessed One was staying near Rājagaha on Vulture Peak Mountain.
snp3.5:1.3 | S: Then the student Māgha approached the Buddha and exchanged greetings with him. | T: Then the young brahman Māgha went to the Blessed One and, on arrival, exchanged courteous greetings with him.
snp3.5:1.4 | S: When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side, | T: After an exchange of friendly greetings & courtesies, he sat to one side. As he was sitting there,
snp3.5:1.5 | S: and said to the Buddha: | T: he said to the Blessed One,
snp3.5:2.1 | S: “I’m a giver, worthy Gotama, a donor; I am bountiful and committed to charity. | T: “Master Gotama, I am generous, a master of giving, magnanimous, responsive to requests.
snp3.5:2.2 | S: I seek wealth in a principled manner, | T: I search for wealth righteously.
snp3.5:2.3 | S: and with that legitimate wealth I give to one person, to two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight, nine, ten, twenty, thirty, forty, fifty, a hundred people or even more. | T: Having searched for wealth righteously, then—with wealth righteously gained, righteously acquired—I give to one, I give to two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight, nine, ten, twenty, thirty, forty, fifty, one hundred, and to more.
snp3.5:2.4 | S: Giving and sacrificing like this, worthy Gotama, do I brim with much merit?” | T: Thus giving, thus sacrificing, do I produce much merit?”
snp3.5:3.1 | S: “Indeed you do, student. | T: “Certainly, young man, thus giving, thus sacrificing, you produce much merit.
snp3.5:3.2 | S: A giver or donor who is bountiful and committed to charity, | T: Anyone who is generous, a master of giving, magnanimous, responsive to requests,
snp3.5:3.3 | S: who seeks wealth in a principled manner, | T: who searches for wealth righteously
snp3.5:3.4 | S: and with that legitimate wealth gives to one person, or up to a hundred people or even more, brims with much merit.” | T: and, having searched for wealth righteously, then—with wealth righteously gained, righteously acquired—gives to one, to two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight, nine, ten, twenty, thirty, forty, fifty, one hundred, and to more, produces much merit.”
snp3.5:3.5 | S: Then Māgha addressed the Buddha in verse: | T: Then the young brahman Māgha addressed the Blessed One in verse:
snp3.5:4.1 | S: “I ask the bountiful Gotama,” | T: “I ask the magnanimous Gotama,
snp3.5:4.2 | S: said Māgha, | T: (none)
snp3.5:4.3 | S: “wearing an ochre robe, wandering homeless. | T: wearing ochre robes, wandering without home:
snp3.5:4.4 | S: Suppose a lay donor who is committed to charity | T: When a householder responsive to requests, a master of giving,
snp3.5:4.5 | S: makes a sacrifice seeking merit, looking for merit, | T: makes a sacrifice in hopes of merit, looking for merit,
snp3.5:4.6 | S: giving food and drink to others here: | T: giving food & drink to others here,
snp3.5:4.7 | S: how is their offering purified?” | T: how is the offering purified for the one making the sacrifice?”
snp3.5:5.1 | S: “Suppose a lay donor who is committed to charity,” | T: The Buddha: “When a householder responsive to requests, a master of giving,
snp3.5:5.2 | S: replied the Buddha, | T: (none)
snp3.5:5.3 | S: “makes a sacrifice seeking merit, looking for merit, | T: makes a sacrifice in hopes of merit, looking for merit,
snp3.5:5.4 | S: giving food and drink to others here: | T: giving food & drink to others here:
snp3.5:5.5 | S: such a one would succeed due to those <j>who are worthy of donations.” | T: Such a person achieves his aim in terms of the recipient.”

